@startuml FIG-CL-TAV-07
skinparam shadowing false
title FIG-CL-TAV-07 Two state machines\nSysML 1.6 notation-based views; executable/metamodel conformance is not claimed\nindependent machines; communication is FIG-CL-TAV-04 ports, not a cross-machine state transition

state Msess as "Msess verification session" {
  [*] --> Idle
  Idle --> Admit
  Admit --> Select : admissible A nonempty
  Admit --> StopBudget : distinguisher or Prep exists but unaffordable
  Admit --> StopNoDistinguisher : no distinguisher and no Prep
  Admit --> StopError : q unknown and Recover not admissible
  Select --> Execute : chosen from A TEST Prep or Recover
  Execute --> Update : valid Izk
  Execute --> ErrorHandle : ERROR
  ErrorHandle --> Admit : retry remaining; unknown-effect only if Recover can enter next A
  ErrorHandle --> StopError : retry cap or Recover not admissible
  Update --> Admit : |Hk| > 1 and selected-mode resource remains
  Update --> StopBudget : selected-mode resource exhausted
  Update --> StopEquivalent : observational equivalence established
  Update --> StopSingleton : |Hk| == 1
  Update --> StopEmpty : Hk empty
  Update --> Stop645 : named 645-blocked item
}

state Mprot as "Mprot protocol black box" {
  state BoundM2 as "bound M2 INFORMATION / UPLOAD\napproved model identity; no new behavior edges"
  state PlannedScope as "planned CRS scope, no behavior edges\nMedia Defined DOWNLOAD\nOperator Defined DOWNLOAD\nFIND"
}

note bottom of Msess
  Stop classes: Stop-Budget, Stop-NoDistinguisher, Stop-Equivalent,
  Stop-Singleton, Stop-Empty, Stop-Error, Stop-645.
  Admit uses the same selected-mode resource rule as FIG-CL-TAV-05.
  ErrorHandle is not an immediate Stop-Error on every ERROR.
  Independent machines. Stimulus and observation use FIG-CL-TAV-04 ports.
  This note is not a state transition between Msess and Mprot.
  New DOWNLOAD/FIND services are not claimed as bound M2 coverage.
end note
@enduml
